// @METADATA:name        = paper_p4
// @METADATA:description = Program P4 from Figure 8 of the paper.
//                         Illustrates observe-nontermination dependence.
//                         observe(x+y>=6) conditions on x and y jointly.
//                         The while loop (line 4) may not terminate when
//                         x=4. Under ns, the while predicate is an obsntd
//                         source and generates obsntd edges to return x.
//                         Under nids, the while predicate is also an
//                         obsntd_nt source but wcd gives fewer edges.
//                         Under ni, only observe is a source.
// @METADATA:reference   = Masud and Olmedo (2026) Static Nontermination-
//                         (In)Sensitive Slicing of Probabilistic Programs.
//                         Figure 8, Program P4.
// @METADATA:criterion   = x
// @METADATA:expected    = ns: observe and while both in slice via obsntd;
//                         nids: observe in slice; while kept via obsntd_nt
//                         with wcd; ni: only observe kept as source;
//                         y always kept via observe dependence on x
// @METADATA:tags        = observe, nontermination, obsntd, paper-example,
//                         figure-8, ns-vs-nids-vs-ni

x :~ unif[1, 4];
y :~ unif[1, 4];
observe(x + y >= 6);
while x = 4 do
    skip;
end
return x;